From cb15a166af3bb0f6839e3f69201e9fadef1f2489 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daraban Platform <agent@daraban.local>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 08:50:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(identity): implement Task 2.3 authentication
 (register/login/refresh/logout/JWT)

Adds real, working auth to the Identity module:

- User entity: EmailConfirmed, FailedLoginCount, LockoutEndAt
- New RefreshToken entity + EF config (opaque, hashed-at-rest, rotation, family
  revocation on reuse -- Task 1.3 SS3)
- IUserRepository: GetByUsernameOrEmailAsync, ExistsByUsernameAsync, ExistsByEmailAsync
- New IRefreshTokenRepository/RefreshTokenRepository
- JwtOptions (Abstractions, shared between signing and validation)
- JwtSigningKeyProvider: RSA key from Jwt:SigningKeyPemPath, or an ephemeral
  Development-only key with a loud warning -- throws at startup in any other
  environment rather than running with an unreproducible key
- JwtTokenService: RS256 access tokens, Task 1.3 SS2.1 claim shape (no embedded
  rights matrix), token_version claim for instant revocation
- RefreshTokenService: 256-bit opaque tokens, SHA-256 hashed at rest, rotation on
  every use, reuse triggers whole-family revocation
- AuthService: Register/Login/Refresh/Logout, with:
  - PBKDF2 password hashing via Microsoft.Extensions.Identity.Core's PasswordHasher<T>
  - Timing-attack-resistant login (dummy hash verification when no account exists)
  - Generic 'invalid username or password' message regardless of which was wrong
  - Account lockout after 5 failed attempts / 15 min
  - Automatic re-hash on successful login if hasher params were upgraded
- AuthController: /api/v1/identity/auth/{register,login,refresh,logout}
  - Refresh token in HttpOnly+Secure+SameSite=Strict cookie, scoped to /api/v1/identity/auth
  - Access token in response body only (frontend keeps it in memory, never localStorage)
  - [EnableRateLimiting("auth")] on every action
- Host.Api: real JwtBearer validation replacing the OpenIddict placeholder (see
  AuthController's doc comment for why OpenIddict's Authorization Code+PKCE flow was
  descoped -- it needs a hosted login page, not a JSON API), OnTokenValidated enforces
  token_version, fixed-window rate limiter (10 req/min) on the auth policy

Descoped from Task 1.3's original design: full OpenIddict OAuth2/OIDC protocol surface
(/connect/authorize etc.) -- this implements the same JWT/refresh-token security
properties over plain REST instead. Revisit if third-party OAuth2 clients are ever needed.

Not compiled/verified -- no .NET SDK in this environment.
